  * latex.js -a doc.tex: if doc.tex is an existing file, treat -a as having no argument

- usage.md and test/api.ts, test/api/node.*js: rename mjs to just js?


- The web component's macros URL is resolved against baseURL, while stylesheet is resolved against the page
- static css is ignored for CustomMacros


- don't use two decorators per macro:
    @Macro('H')
    @Args(...)
  consolidate it to one:
    @HMacro(<args>)
    @VMacro(...)
    @HVMacro(...)
    @PMacro(...)


- check out LinkeDom (or Happy-DOM) and see if it works with LaTeX.js
  both have no SVG font metrics - do I even need that (getBBox)?
  
- in the unit tests: check the (serialized) html for validity

import { HtmlValidate } from "html-validate";

const htmlvalidate = new HtmlValidate({
  extends: ["html-validate:recommended"],
});

const report = await htmlvalidate.validateString("<p><div>invalid</div></p>");

console.log(report.valid); // false
console.log(report.results[0].messages);
